// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/chat_probe.t27 -- drives chat_host.t27 the way a window would, with no screen: two processes on
// 127.0.0.1, each with its own HOME (its own ~/.t27os identity, friends and chat log). Not part of the app; a pass
// means the chat core carries messages over a message session, not that a chat screen works. Refs
// gHashTag/t27#11560.
// Runs (one line per check; exit 0 only when every check passed):
//   CHP_ROLE=id            open (or make) the identity of $HOME, add CHP_FRIEND (an invite string) to its friends
//                          when given, print "INVITE <invite>".
//   CHP_ROLE=a             the first friend of $HOME's table is the peer, at CHP_PEER (127.0.0.1) : CHP_PEER_PORT;
//                          this side binds CHP_PORT. Sends CHP_N (20) messages: number 7 is 1500 bytes of Cyrillic
//                          (3 parts, cut inside characters), number 12 holds an emoji, number 3 holds U+202E (the
//                          override that shows "gpj.exe" as "exe.jpg"; cleaned on send, chat_core ch_clean). CHP_RAW=1
//                          puts the U+202E back into the stored line after the send, as a client that does not clean
//                          would send it, so the receiver's cleaning is what is measured. CHP_DROP=n drops this side's
//                          n-th text frame as a lost datagram. Waits for CHP_R (5) replies, opens the chat (READ),
//                          then for the idle close.
//   CHP_ROLE=b             the same peer setup; once all CHP_N messages are here it opens the chat and replies
//                          CHP_R times, then waits for the idle close.
//   Both sides then save, read their log back from disk and check: every line once, in order, the texts, every
//   outgoing line READ, no unread left, the message socket closed in a started process (FD_CLOEXEC), no video control
//   sent by the message session, and the counters (frames, resends, ACKs, duplicates) are printed.
// Build (Apple silicon):
//   t27b build specs/t27os/chat_probe.t27 -o chp.o --macho
//   ld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 $(xcrun --show-sdk-version) -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) \
//      -e _main -lSystem -lffi -framework CoreFoundation -framework Security -framework AudioToolbox \
//      -framework CoreGraphics -framework ImageIO -o chp chp.o
//   A: CHP_ROLE=id HOME=$HA; B: CHP_ROLE=id HOME=$HB CHP_FRIEND=<A's invite>; again A with CHP_FRIEND=<B's invite>;
//   then B with CHP_ROLE=b CHP_PORT=47812 CHP_PEER_PORT=47811 and A with CHP_ROLE=a CHP_PORT=47811
//   CHP_PEER_PORT=47812 CHP_DROP=5. Each run ends with an idle close (about 32 s).
module T27osChatProbe;

